/*
  protocol/blake_calc.spthy -- PROTOCOL LAYER, Blake's CALC_SK, DEFAULT (Attentive) answer.
  Pulled in by ceremony.base.spthy, so every experiment gets it unless it opts out.

  Blake answers his CALC_SK Attentively: the correct kdf(Na,Nb), exactly the key the old inline
  B_recv_Na_send_Nb produced. The action facts Calc('Blake','Attentive') and Key('Blake',kdf(Na,Nb))
  are preserved, so the agreement / completion lemmas are unaffected.

  This DEFAULT deliberately does NOT post a persistent !Req('Blake',...): the stressor detectors
  read !Req (sigma1 on 'Hard'; sigma2 UNCONDITIONALLY on any !Req), so a !Req here would let them
  fire for Blake inside every existing experiment and change its behaviour. By computing inline off
  the linear BlakeWait, Blake stays INERT to the human layer -- Attentive in every existing
  experiment, with no state-space growth. To put Blake under stress, an experiment pulls
  protocol/blake_calc_stressable.spthy (which DOES post a !Req) instead of this file.
*/

rule B_calc_attentive:
    [ BlakeWait(idB, <Na,Nb>) ]
  --[ Calc('Blake','Attentive'), Key('Blake', kdf(Na,Nb)) ]->
    [ BlakeDone(idB, kdf(Na,Nb)) ]
